TI  - NCI Cancer Research Data Commons: Core Standards and Services.
PG  - 1384-1387
LID - 10.1158/0008-5472.CAN-23-2655 [doi]
AB  - The NCI Cancer Research Data Commons (CRDC) is a collection of data commons, 
      analysis platforms, and tools that make existing cancer data more findable and 
      accessible by the cancer research community. In practice, the two biggest hurdles 
      to finding and using data for discovery are the wide variety of models and 
      ontologies used to describe data, and the dispersed storage of that data. Here, 
      we outline core CRDC services to aggregate descriptive information from multiple 
      studies for findability via a single interface and to provide a single access 
      method that spans multiple data commons. See related articles by Wang et al., p. 
      1388, Pot et al., p. 1396, and Kim et al., p. 1404.
